ess had only been  with her acting agency for one month  before she'd gotten the opportunity to  submit a self-tape for the netflix hit  it was the very first audition she'd  done by tape and had a ton of nerves  going in but in the midst of her frantic  prep she dove into the script and turned  out what happened to be a tape good  enough to earn her an in-person audition  in korea what makes this even more  impressive is the fact that she was busy  doing fashion week in new york when the  request came to her but once the  callback came she hopped on a flight to  korea nerves ran high for the actress  and the experience of being in the room  with the director was intense she even  had to stop drinking coffee because of  the anxiety all this caused  while by this point she was already  playing sebiak and doing a lot of  research on north korean defectors to  prep for her role the actress wasn't so  confident so she requested dinner with  director huang to make sure they were on  the same page and she was meeting  expectations  of course she was blowing it out of the  water and huang was able to confirm with  her that she was a great actress and the  perfect one to play the complex and  strong character  if it seems like the guillen actor  suited his role perfectly it's probably  because the part was actually written  specifically for him  director huang had hoped the incredible  actor would accept the offer to play the  role and luckily for everyone he said  yes the decision was pretty easy since  the actor had always wanted to work with  the director  the incredible story lines in the script  made the answer pretty easy as well when  it came to preparing for the role the  relationship between him and sang wu was  important so the actors actually spent a  lot of time together bonding and  drinking wine this sounds like pretty  great acting prep to us  while he wasn't the first choice to play  ali anubham tripathi definitely made an  impact with his portrayal on squid game  the actor originally from india actually  studied acting in south korea and in  january 2020 a korean casting agency  reached out to him and he sent in his  tape for squid game  once he'd had his in-person audition  with the director and showed off his  emotional acting the actor was booked he  went hard at work with research and  preparing to play a pakistani character  truthfully i asked my pakistani friends  and all to help me with the language in  fact it was his internal quest all the  way from the day they said yes his  enthusiasm and commitment no doubt made  him an excellent addition to the show  we're definitely glad he was part of  this cast even if ali didn't get what he  deserved in the series  easy in a sense like okay i got the role  hard because i have to prepare for the  role hajin was honored to be part of  squid game especially because of how  much he wanted it when he first went in  to audition having wanted to move  towards more serious work instead of the  usual rom-coms he'd been performing in  the actor was overwhelmed by the idea of  working on such an incredible korean  project with amazing talent attached he  made sure to give it his best in the  audition and luckily it left an  impression while he knew the police  officer was a smaller role the storyline  really intrigued him and he worked a lot  to make sure he explored the internal  struggle in his character and depicted  how much he tried to achieve justice  this wasn't the first time the duksu  actor and creator of squid game have  worked together the two collaborated on  the 2017 film the fortress director  huang had no trouble picturing this  incredible actor as the menacing doksu  since the actor often plays gang members  the creator did end up apologizing to  the actor for giving him yet another  tough credit we have a feeling the  performer was very much okay with this  one though the fact that the actor is  the opposite of his character in real  life is a testament to his 